  "description": "Compact. Versatile and now with electric assistance. Anything but Ordinary.\nThe Skyline E blends the fit and feel of a full-size bicycle with the sharp handling, practicality, and fun-factor of 20″ wheels with the added benefit of controlled and powerful electric assistance provided by a Mahle XS electric drive system. Hand-built in Stratford-upon-Avon, it’s designed to make every ride feel fresh — turning heads on the commute, firing you up off-road, or just giving you that grin-per-mile feeling on a chilled city cruise.\nEasy to tuck away in a hallway or apartment and simple to throw in the back of a car or train, it’s built for riders who want a bike that fits their life as well as their adventures. Thread it through the rush of London, Tokyo, or New York and feel it dart effortlessly between traffic lights. Load it with racks and knobbly tyres and it becomes a ready-for-anything sidekick for gravel tracks, forest paths, and mountain trails, where the smaller wheels turn every climb, descent, and twist into part of the adventure. Or keep it pared-back for a laid-back roll around town — the kind of ride where you roll slow, soak up the atmosphere, and still turn heads with that unmistakable Pashley style.\nWherever you take it, the Skyline makes the ride feel brighter, sharper, and far more alive.",
